WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.610
- This line wraps around three times

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.560
before it starts going straight.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.030
- [Narrator] If you've traveled recently

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.970
you've likely seen long lines
and stranded passengers.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.120
- Airports will definitely
be significantly busier

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.370
than summer of 2021.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.530
- [Narrator] Inflation is
also pumping up the price

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.470
of everything from food
to flights, to gas.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.690
So to help you save money and time,

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.300
Wall Street Journal Travel
Columnist, Dawn Gilbertson

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.663
has three tips to help you
navigate this busy travel season.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.200
Number one, plan ahead to save time

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.360
and alleviate stress at the airport.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.810
- One option, a lot of flyers
don't seem to be aware of yet

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.930
is a relatively new program
that allows you to reserve

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.230
a spot in the security line for free.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.480
- [Narrator] This program is
offered at several airports,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.670
including those in Seattle, Los Angeles,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.050
and Newark New Jersey.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.030
Each airport has its own protocols

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.760
but generally travelers
can sign up for 15 minutes

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.240
security appointments up to
72 hours before their flights.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.760
Once at the airport, you show a QR code

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.070
and enter designated
checkpoint lanes that take you

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.140
to the front of the general security line.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.080
- The Phoenix Airport, for
example, told me that people

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.510
who have used that line
on average report saving

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.570
at least 20 minutes in
the security checkpoint

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.060
- [Narrator] TSA pre-check
and Clear can also save time

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.370
but they charge membership fees.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.110
Another time saving option,

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.590
a relatively new feature at
airport Starbucks locations.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.590
- You can now do mobile
ordering at the airport

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.160
and anybody who's seen a
Starbucks line at a major airport

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.900
or even a smaller airport, you know,

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.480
knows sometimes they can rival the lines

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.280
at the TSA checkpoint

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.500
- Use the Starbucks mobile
app to skip the line

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.670
and place your order.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.230
I placed my order at 5:08

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.570
and I received my coffee at 5:14.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:43.950
- [Narrator] And for those renting cars,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.500
you can also take advantage
of line skipping options

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.473
by signing up for rental
agencies loyalty programs.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.590
Tip number two, if something goes wrong

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.320
like your flight gets
canceled, act quickly.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.820
- Don't just do one thing.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.710
You know, if you're
gonna go get in that line

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.380
while you're in that line, get
on the airlines mobile app.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.390
Look at other options at the airport.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.890
- [Narrator] United Airlines, for example

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.230
has a new tool called, Agent on Demand,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.720
which connects travelers
with customer service agents

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.960
in other cities as a way to
speed up the rebooking process.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.950
- I'm also a very big fan
of reaching out to airlines

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.290
on Twitter, direct message.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.970
They tend to get back to you quicker.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.670
You start the conversation
about rebooking.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.440
- [Narrator] Another
thing to keep in mind is,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.090
if an airline cancels your flight

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.090
and gives you your money back,
that refund might not cover

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.010
the cost of a new flight this summer.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.100
- Do not ask for that refund, you know

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.540
so that you can book on another airline

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.840
until you shop another
airline because that flight

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.510
could be three times
the price that you paid.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.310
So this summer, in a lot of cases

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.520
you have to weigh the
airlines rebooking option.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.350
- [Narrator] Finally, shop around.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.510
- If you haven't booked
your airline tickets yet,

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.563
maybe check out some of the newer airlines

00:02:54.563 --> 00:02:57.690
that have launched during the pandemic.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.920
A couple that come to mind
are Avelo and Breeze Airways.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.660
Since not everybody has heard of them

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.870
you might have a better
chance at seat availability.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.090
- [Narrator] Both airlines
follow the model of discounters

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.623
like Allegiant and Frontier.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.820
Avelo operates flights out
of new Haven, Los Angeles

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.840
and Orlando.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.900
And Breeze Airways focuses on
mid-size cities like Hartford,

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.510
Connecticut, and
Charleston, South Carolina.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.697
- Check their websites
because a lot of times

00:03:23.697 --> 00:03:26.280
the tickets are significantly cheaper.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.740
Both airlines have relatively new planes,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.880
experienced executives, and
some routes you can fly nonstop

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.580
and skip the connecting airport drama.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.740
- [Narrator] But keep in mind
that these smaller airlines

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.780
might not have as many flight options.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.810
- On most routes, they
don't fly every single day.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.570
So, you know, in times of flight troubles

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.660
you might not be able to get
out as quickly as you want.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.430
- [Narrator] If you're going
on a road trip you might

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.280
be able to save money on
gas by using the same tools

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.300
you use at home.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.790
- If you have a Costco
membership, you know

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.980
Walmart also has a membership program.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.920
You know, you can use
those savings on the road.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.090
GasBuddy is one of the apps
that a lot of people download

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.020
before a trip, it'll find
the lowest gas in your area.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.850
- [Narrator] But
regardless of where or how

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.170
you plan to travel this summer.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.720
- Have a backup plan, maybe
a couple backup plans.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.120
You know, we've all seen
the headlines on the number

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.370
of canceled flights and delayed flights.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.213
So just look at your
options before you take off.

